---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const faqs = [
  ['What is the main Dext alternative for Xero practices?', 'Hubdoc. It is included with qualifying Xero plans (standalone about $12 per month) and covers email, mobile and upload capture that publishes into Xero.'],
  ['When should a firm stay on Dext instead of Hubdoc?', 'Stay on Dext if you run mixed Xero and QuickBooks (or other) ledgers on one capture stack, or rely on bank-statement, line-item or supplier-statement extraction beyond basic OCR.'],
  ['Is Booke AI a replacement for Dext?', 'Only partly. Booke AI does OCR for bills and receipts plus daily bank categorization inside QuickBooks Online or Xero, at $129 per business per month (firm and white-label plans by quote). It is built for coding and exception review, not practice-wide capture.'],
  ['Does a Xero partner pay for a Hubdoc practice account?', 'No. Xero partners can get a free Hubdoc practice account.'],
];
const faqLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })),
});
---
<Base
  title="Dext alternatives for bookkeeping firms — receipt capture options"
  description="Looking past Dext for receipt and bill capture? Compare Hubdoc and other firm-fit options for Xero and QuickBooks practices. Pricing verified Oct 2026."
>
  <h1>Dext alternatives</h1>
  <p>Firms leave or skip Dext when clients are already on Xero (and capture is included), when per-client partner pricing does not fit a small list, or when they want categorization and OCR in one tool rather than a dedicated capture product. Below are the closest options in our directory — not a full market scan.</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Alternative</th>
        <th>Best fit vs Dext</th>
        <th>Pricing (verified Oct 2026)</th>
        <th>Trade-off</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/hubdoc`}>Hubdoc</a></td>
        <td>Primary alternative for receipt/bill capture on Xero practices</td>
        <td>Included with qualifying Xero plans; standalone ~$12/mo</td>
        <td>Strongest on Xero; fewer multi-ledger and extraction-credit options than Dext</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/booke-ai`}>Booke AI</a></td>
        <td>Partial overlap: OCR for bills/receipts plus daily bank categorization inside QBO/Xero</td>
        <td>Business $129/business/mo; firm/white-label by quote</td>
        <td>Not a pure Dext replacement — built for coding and exception review, not practice-wide capture credits</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>When Hubdoc is enough</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Most clients sit on paid Xero plans where Hubdoc (or Smart Document Capture) is already included.</li>
    <li>You mainly need email/mobile/upload capture and publish into Xero, not bank-statement or line-item extraction packs.</li>
    <li>You want a free Hubdoc practice account as a Xero partner.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to stay on Dext</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You run mixed Xero and QuickBooks (or other) ledgers and need one capture stack.</li>
    <li>You rely on bank-statement, line-item, or supplier-statement extraction beyond basic OCR.</li>
    <li>Partner Essentials/Advanced plans and practice workflows matter more than Xero-bundled pricing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When Booke AI is the better next step</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Capture is secondary; the pain is uncategorized bank lines and chasing missing docs after OCR.</li>
    <li>You want AI bookkeeping inside QBO/Xero with exception review, not a standalone document inbox.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (<><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></>))}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLd} />

  <p>
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/compare/dext-vs-hubdoc/`}>Dext vs Hubdoc (head-to-head)</a>
    · <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/dext`}>Dext Prepare</a>
    · <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/category/receipt-capture`}>All receipt &amp; document capture tools</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
